<urn:atm:triage:finding/RRG-BENCH-READ-PRECOND-001>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "RRG-BENCH-READ-PRECOND-001" ;
  triage:title "just benchmark-read requires an account-local serving daemon on the benchmark account, which the atmbench account does not run, so the read/query family has been unavailable on every readiness attempt" ;
  triage:description "Release-readiness plan section 3.2 lists just benchmark-read (read-fanout, query-fts, read-under-write-load) as a required family with evidence under site/reports/read-query-benchmark/. On every 1.4.x attempt on rand-m5/atmbench (1.4.7 through 1.4.10) arch-ctm reports the family unavailable: scripts/smoke/read_benchmark.py execute() resolves a release atm binary (_atm_binary, line 260) and drives it with ATM_IDENTITY=av4-driver against whatever daemon serves that account's Unix HTTP socket; unlike run_admission_capacity.py it never starts a fixture daemon, and the atmbench account only ever has the send benchmark's disposable fixture daemons, so the CLI reports no serving Unix HTTP socket and the family never runs. Classification: benchmark-harness / process precondition, blocking for the read family only (the send family is unaffected). The plan text does not state the precondition. Resolution options, smallest first: (a) document and provision an account-local 1.4.x daemon on atmbench for the duration of the read campaign (release-readiness process step, no harness code), or (b) make read_benchmark.py start and tear down its own fixture daemon the way the send runner does. arch-ctm picks (a) unless the runner's ambient-state refusal makes it impossible, in which case (b) with the minimal change; the plan section 3.2 must gain the precondition either way." ;
  triage:phaseId "readiness-1.4" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "benchmark-harness" ;
  triage:severity "blocking" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "file_only" ;
  triage:status "fixed" ;
  triage:dispatchReady false ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-09-03T19:05:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:foundIn triage:RRG-S1 ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-09-03T18:36:28Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/RRG-BENCH-READ-PRECOND-001/CAND-1> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/RRG-BENCH-READ-PRECOND-001/CAND-2> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/RRG-BENCH-READ-PRECOND-001/QMGR-CLOSE-1> ;
  triage:closedAt "2026-09-03T22:15:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:closedBy "quality-mgr" ;
  triage:triageRecordVersion "2" .

